API.md §5.7: a fix is offered only when every importer of the field's package is loaded: t imports a and is not selected, so a gets the finding and no fix.
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- select --
a
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// Item.
record Item {
  /// Level.
  dwLevel: Int
}
-- t/t.canon --
package t

import a

@text("doc.txt")
export fn doc() -> a.Item {
  return a.Item { dwLevel: 1 }
}
-- findings.txt --
warning[W0001]  a/a.canon:6:3
  field dwLevel keeps the legacy prefix dw in its Canon name: rename it level (canon rename keeps the old wire name with @json where a load or a data emit reads the field)

0 errors, 1 warning in 1 package (…)
